{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Basil","id":"339235123759153162","is_bot":0,"username":"divinedefault"},"author_id":"339235123759153162","channel_id":"850779383656218636","content":"pc's haven't exceeded 7th level which only goes up to 4th level spells. and players are typically seen as exceptional","created_at":"2021-08-13T14:46:30.065000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"875752178592124979","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"850779383656218636","content":"Most npcs are of a level that a few pcs might have an issue, but many pcs would stomp.\n\nI could name a handful of npcs that are at or above lvl 17... or cr 12ish.\n\nIt would be reasonable to assume 98 percent of a fantasy population is lvl 1 or below.\n\nAfter that its more thank likely a curve by tier.  You have twice as many tier 1 as tier 2, tier 3 is half of 2, and 4 half of three.\n\nSo if there are 10 npcs in tier 4, then 20 in tier 3, 40 tier 2, and 80 tier 1. (Its more likely twice that number overall and a lot of it is unnamed, but it would be a fair assumption to population breakdowns)\n\nAlso reminder, CR is meant for ~5 players of that level to have a challenging, but not deadly fight.  So CR10 is a lot more powerful than level 10.","created_at":"2021-08-13T15:20:48.486000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"875760812235571250","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
